  "kind": "definition",
  "title": "Subgroup schemes",
  "statement": "Let $G$ be a group scheme over a\nfield $k$. A *closed subgroup scheme* of $G$ is a closed\nsubscheme $Z\\subseteq G$ such that for every $k$-algebra $R$ the\nsubset $Z(R)\\subseteq G(R)$ is a subgroup of the group $G(R)$. A\n*subgroup scheme* of $G$ is a $k$-group scheme $Z$ together\nwith a homomorphism $i:Z\\to G$ whose\ninduced maps $i(R):Z(R)\\to G(R)$ are injective for every $k$-algebra\n$R$. The subgroup scheme is *normal* if $i(R)(Z(R))$ is a\nnormal subgroup of $G(R)$ for every $R$.",
